  "name": "Example: Calculating the Cross Product of Two Parallel Vectors",
  "problem": "The vector $\\mathbf{a}$ has magnitude $4,$ the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ has magnitude $6,$ and $\\mathbf{a} \\parallel \\mathbf{b}.$ Find $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose $\\mathbf a$ and $\\mathbf b$ are nonzero vectors. Then, $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}$ if and only if $\\mathbf{a} \\parallel \\mathbf{b}.$\n\nTherefore, $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}.$",
